WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.840
This is the Singularity Daily, for Saturday, November 28.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.010
Here's your day in superintelligence, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.860
Who's cooking? Mark Zuckerberg had Meta's AI agent smoke his turkey,

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.510
while he played GTA 6.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.220
His wife conceded their annual turkey contest, and asked Muse to do hers.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.620
In Britain,

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:37.530
an AI agent paid for nine pizzas straight from a bank account. No card.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.780
The payments boss behind it says this is po

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.120
ssibly the last Black Friday as we know it.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.580
Meanwhile,

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:52.410
Bloomberg says one of Nvidia's most powerful AI racks turned up in a Shanghai data center.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.630
Jensen Huang once said they were too big to smuggle.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.960
They can weigh over 1,500 kilos.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.090
Now, the money. Anthropic's shares jumped 8% on Friday,

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.180
back above their IPO price.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.120
Economists think South Korea's chip-fuelled exports nearly doubled in November.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.800
Fastest in over 50 years.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.540
Germany's SAP is reportedly weighing at least 10,000 job cuts,

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.920
in an AI shake-up.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.110
Oh, and Tesla's filed to buy assets from EMAG,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.060
a German maker of machines for robot gears.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.900
In mice, Tencent's AI-designed drug beat Wegovy's ingredient for weight loss,

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.430
at a tenth of the dose.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.140
Another of its designs left tumours 94% smaller.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.870
Still early days, and only in mice.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.480
The catch? Outside Anthropic's office,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.460
a hunger strike against self-improving AI just hit day five.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.420
And LA schools quietly switched off Google's AI answers.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.520
In Russia,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.860
Yandex reportedly plans to pilot humanoid robot deliveries before the year is out.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.610
A rover drives your parcel to the door, then a humanoid carries it inside.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.590
And a German startup's chips now do AI math with light, in a real data center.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.080
So, who's cooking? Let the machines do it,

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.720
sure. Just make sure everyone gets a plate.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.540
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.
